open.question:
You are in a design review for an LLM customer-support agent that uses function calling. It exposes a single tool:

```json
{
  "name": "manage_ticket",
  "description": "Manage a support ticket.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "action":    { "type": "string" },
      "ticket_id": { "type": "string" },
      "priority":  { "type": "string" },
      "data":      { "type": "object" }
    }
  }
}
```

Telemetry shows recurring failures: the model calls it with `action` values the backend rejects (`"close"` instead of `"resolve"`); it sometimes omits `ticket_id`; it invents priorities like `"urgent"` when the backend only accepts `P0`–`P3`; it stuffs arbitrary keys into `data`; and it uses this same mutating path to *read* a ticket's status. Redesign the tool interface and the surrounding validation/dispatch layer so the agent calls it reliably. Justify each change by the concrete mechanism it fixes, and be explicit about what the schema can enforce versus what your dispatcher must still enforce at runtime.

